WEBVTT

00:07:59.636 --> 00:08:01.076
(Laughter)

00:08:01.076 --> 00:08:03.436
That's also a picture I took
on my phone recently.

00:08:03.436 --> 00:08:04.596
(Laughter)

00:08:04.636 --> 00:08:06.436
It's been a funny old week.

00:08:06.796 --> 00:08:08.116
That's ...

00:08:08.636 --> 00:08:11.756
That’s the kind of image
your imagination puts into your head

00:08:11.796 --> 00:08:14.316
when you think deep sea, tentacles
and the rest of it.

00:08:14.316 --> 00:08:15.876
The reality of the matter is --

00:08:15.876 --> 00:08:20.116
and I can proudly say that I discovered
the deepest octopus in the world --

00:08:20.756 --> 00:08:22.476
Audience: Aw.

00:08:22.516 --> 00:08:24.436
AJ: It’s the size of a puppy, too.

00:08:24.436 --> 00:08:25.916
(Laughter)

00:08:26.396 --> 00:08:27.556
It gets better.

00:08:27.596 --> 00:08:30.116
Its real name is Grimpoteuthis,
which is a bit “rurr.”